From bac94bd3246d88bba584201fdf205e4481306aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:44:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] fix(agent): guard structural turn-completion stalls

A model can end a turn with prose announcing its next action and no tool
call, silently stopping the task. The existing English/Russian phrase list
does not generalise to languages without tense/modals (Chinese), so port
OpenClaw's structural, language-independent guards instead.

- prompt: emit an "EXECUTION BIAS" block in writeToolInstructionsSection
  when tools are enabled, so a turn that only promises future work takes
  the next action in the same turn. Guarded on tools.len > 0 so tool-less
  prompts are untouched.
- providers: record finish_reason=="tool_calls" (OpenAI-compatible) and
  stop_reason=="tool_use" (Anthropic) as ChatResponse.finish_tool_use,
  read from provider output structure, never assistant prose.
- providers/sse: on the streaming path (native tool calls while streaming,
  #971) set StreamChatResult.finish_tool_use from a streamed finish_reason
  "tool_calls", scanned textually as the twin of sseLineReportsLengthFinish
  so a >16 KB data line cannot hide it. It is set only when the calls were
  trusted (the stream ended cleanly) and the stream was not truncated, so a
  call cut mid-flight or a max_tokens cut never reports a tool stop.
- agent: when finish_tool_use is set but no call was parsed, nudge once
  and then fail with error.NoResponseContent (already user-visible) rather
  than returning nothing. The streamed flag reaches the same branch, so a
  streaming tool stop is guarded identically to the non-streaming parsers.
  Also pick targeted nudges for settled-tools-with-no-answer and
  reasoning-only empty turns (cap 2) instead of the web-search text,
  reusing the existing empty-response retry budget.

The English/Russian shouldForceActionFollowThrough list is unchanged.
